1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,000
Choose the lower-side label. Select Click once. The first control describes how YOU press the button.

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:14,126
Open the action chooser. Pick Desktop left. This is what the APP will do after your button press.

3
00:00:14,126 --> 00:00:21,126
Save for all apps. Lower-side single click now has Desktop left as its saved action.

4
00:00:21,126 --> 00:00:28,126
Choose the upper-side label. Set Click once → Desktop right, then Save for all apps.

5
00:00:28,126 --> 00:00:35,126
Choose Hold → Mission Control and save. The same button can have separate click and hold actions.

6
00:00:35,126 --> 00:00:44,126
Double click can use a third action. It adds a short wait so single and double clicks can be distinguished.

7
00:00:44,126 --> 00:00:51,126
Buttons 1 and 2 support double click and hold. Ordinary left/right clicks and dragging stay available.
